do-- cognitive tasks, thinking tasks, and things like that. And so the most common, sensical way to do that is to say, well, if I want the computer to do something complicated, like play chess, I'm just going to sit down with a few chess grandmasters, show them a whole bunch of board moves, and ask them how they figure out how to respond, how to play the next move. I'm going to sit down and talk to all these people, and then I'm going to write down a whole bunch of rules. If this is the board position, move this.

5
