not pervasively successful? Why was it not pervasively successful? It seems like a pretty good idea to me. And the people who came up with these things are smart people. They're not dumb people. They know what they're doing. So why did it not work? AUDIENCE: Because it's time-intensive, so in the case that you have to run through all these scenarios that can ever exist, and still some new scenarios can come up that you didn't cater for [INAUDIBLE. ] RAMA RAMAKRISHNAN: Right. So there are two aspects to what you said,

